WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.220
[Intro music]

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.920
You don't happen to own a cat, do you?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.760
Well, almost owning a cat doesn't do me any good.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.400
Yeah, I have a bit of a weird question for you. Do you have a cat?

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.320
All right, do you have any like really close friends who have cats?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.600
Hank, I think we're gonna have to wait till Thursday on the cat licking.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.840
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday August 14th,

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.440
the day of my punishment.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.660
Hi, can I have a hamburger happy meal please with an orange drink?

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.140
[Cashier]: Boy or girl?

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.820
Is it for a boy or a girl?

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.020
Uh, a girl.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.320
We have gender-specific happy meals now. I don't think this represents progress, Hank.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.940
How do you think this is gonna go?

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.420
[Sarah]: I think it's gonna go better than the chin wax.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.560
Okay, with like one being

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:53.660
a baby pinched me and ten being I just waxed my chin, where do you think the pain is gonna fall?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.000
[Sarah]: Five.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.300
You think it's a five.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.580
All right Hank, welcome to cooking with John Green.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:05.720
Now I'm going to blend a happy meal. I got the orange drink. Something just told me that it was going to be better.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.420
We're putting in some of the orange drink,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.400
I'm going to save a little bit to help wash down the rest of what I'm about to do.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.500
Open it up.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.380
French fries.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.720
Oh god, it's already gross.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.080
Hamburger.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.040
It's quite a lot of food actually!

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.760
We're ready to blend!

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.340
[Blender whirring]

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:37.920
Oh that, that just looks delicious. Like all the best parts of food plus all the best parts of liquid.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.900
I see little bits of gristle, that's nice.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.520
Ah God. [Sarah laughing.]

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:52.700
It just, just doesn't smell like something that you should be eating with a spoon.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.440
[Sarah laughing]

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.060
I think I'm gonna puke. I only got one spoon in and I feel like puking.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.600
[Sarah]: Eat spoonful after spoonful.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.640
[Kenesaw Mountain Landis - Jonathan Coulton playing]

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.820
[Sarah laughing]

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:20.700
[Music keeps playing]

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.220
[Sarah laughing]

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:46.240
[Music keeps playing]

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.240
[John retching]

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.800
[Music keeps playing]

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.620
I'm really glad I didn't say say I'd eat a McDonald's extra value meal because that would have killed me.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.740
I can see a little bit of pickle.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.180
FINISHED.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.860
No more happy meal.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.760
No matter how much this hurts, little man, it's not going to be as bad as the last thing.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:16.420
If you'd told me on January 1st 2007 that we would be doing this, I would not have believed you.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.800
1, 2, 3, [wax rips], OHH! BOY!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:27.020
Wow! That was not a five. That is not a five!

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:27.600
[Wax rips]

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.720
WUGGH.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.260
[Wax rips]

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.980
NNNNNNGGGG.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.480
[Wax rips]

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.080
OOO

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.880
[Wax rips]

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.540
[Wax rips]

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.400
[Wax rips]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.040
[Wax rips]

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:43.540
I would rather wax my entire body, head to toe, than ever eat a blenderized Happy Meal ever again.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:44.460
[Wax rips]

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.180
[Wax rips]

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:45.720
[Wax rips]

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.220
[Wax rips]

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:46.720
[Wax rips]

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.220
[Wax rips]

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.280
Last one.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.940
One, two, three,

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:50.980
[Wax rips] HOO-AA

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:54.440
Hank, I have done some serious waxing.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.540
And I'll see you singing tomorrow.

